<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25072" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Issa</span></b> , ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἴσσα,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an island in the
				Adriatic Sea</i>, <i>near Illyria</i>, <i>with a town of the same name</i>, now <i>Lissa</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 26, 30, § 152</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Caes. B.
				C. 3, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 43, 9</span></i>. —
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Issaeus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Issa</i>, <i>Issæan;
				subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Issaei</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Issa</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 31,
			45</span></i>. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Issaĭcus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>Issæan</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 32,
			21</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Issensis</span></b> , e,
				adj., <i>Issæan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">naves,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					43, 9</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Issenses</span></b> , ium, m.,
				<i>the inhabitants of Issa</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 45,
			26</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
